WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit
1: Daily Life & Communication.

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.580
Welcome to Year 4 English!

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.820
In this unit you will explore daily life and communication —

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.100
the things people do every day and the
ways we share ideas with one another.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.780
You will read about routines, letters
and mail, working hard, and being fair.

6
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:27.880
You will learn how people communicate in different
languages, and why steady effort helps us gain new skills.

7
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:34.260
By the end, you will be able to interview someone about
their daily work, write clearly about your own routine,

8
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:40.100
and use new grammar to make your sentences stronger
— just like Sophia does in this unit's story.

9
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:46.320
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:53.540
By the end of this unit, you will be able to talk and write
about your daily routine and the things you do every day.

11
00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:00.540
you will also explain why communication — letters,
mail, and language — matters to a community.

12
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:06.320
you will also use verb patterns correctly
(for example, “she agrees to send the mail”).

13
00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.100
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:16.640
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
mail, language, citizen, agree, continue, gain.

15
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:22.540
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.980
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.080
The reading sequence includes A Day
at the Posthouse and My Daily Routine.

18
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:32.740
Read actively.

19
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.540
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.620
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.380
The first language focus is Verb Patterns.

22
00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.040
A verb pattern is the way we join a
verb to the word that comes after it.

23
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:58.100
Some verbs are followed by to + another verb,
and some are followed by a verb ending in -ing.

24
00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.600
Getting the pattern right makes your sentences clear.

25
00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:08.360
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

26
00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.940
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Describe Your Daily Routine.

27
00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:19.260
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

28
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.520
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

29
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.260
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

30
00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.180
You are ready to begin.

31
00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:36.180
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

32
00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.240
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

33
00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:45.200
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
